ts. These are observed mechanisms, not proof of adequate quorum or agreement.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-propose\",\n        \"B-preaccept\",\n        \"B-form\",\n        \"B-accept\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-execute\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-value\",\n        \"F-decision\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-phase1\",\n        \"S-pre-reply\",\n        \"S-accept\",\n        \"S-commit\",\n        \"S-exec\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Authority is per instance. Initial ballot is row owner ID. Recovery preserves proposals, resets bookkeeping and chooses a ballot congruent to the recovering replica, with higher-ballot adjustment conditional on IsLeader. Prepare raises a remote promise and returns retained value context. Initiator instead raises both promise and value ballot before self report. Matching Prepare replies fill a recovery quorum; maximum value ballot selects history, then status determines committed retention, Accept or restarted PreAccept. Master role assignment enables retry behavior but is not exclusive proposal ownership. Lower-ballot requests and mismatched replies are filtered; already queued messages remain independently dispatched.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-select\",\n        \"B-recover-trigger\",\n        \"B-transport\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-value\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-recovery\",\n        \"S-exec-recovery\",\n        \"S-dispatch\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The same local command/status/value-ballot record is both formed by proposal/accept/commit and consumed by later authority acquisition. Recovery is meant to carry eligible prior support into new formation: accepted selection re-enters Accept, committed selection stays committed, other selection restarts phase 1. Default execution detects stalled known instances and enqueues recovery. Local committed guards protect some old decisions, but report production/selection determines whether a new owner discovers another replica's decision. This producer-consumer distinction supplies the first question.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-propose\",\n        \"B-accept\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-select\",\n        \"B-recover-trigger\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-value\",\n        \"F-decision\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-phase1\",\n        \"S-accept\",\n        \"S-commit\",\n        \"S-recovery\",\n        \"S-exec-recovery\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Legal recovery history discriminating self-report promotion from prior committed support remains to construct.\",\n      \"Independent quorum, Accept status, optional persistence and SCAN leads remain sourced surfaces.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Both core relationships and their connection are traced through read handlers, actual transport dispatch, recovery trigger, membership inputs and execution consumer. Local anomalies remain explicit; usable is navigation readiness, not correctness.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"ec73e1f00e0745d19e8e5bb7a44f5a28\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"ec73e1f00e0745d19e8e5bb7a44f5a28\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bfd4b4a4056c40faa569717328cf6a6d\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\"